<title>ITALY: Italy's Perugia sees June CPI at 0.4 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Perugia sees June CPI at 0.4 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PERUGIA, Italy 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Perugia said its June consumer price index rose 0.4 percent month-on-month and 1.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In May, Perugia's inflation rate stood at 0.3 and 1.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Perugia is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Friday and Monday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 1.26 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to May 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.4    (0.3)    1.4  (1.2)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0   (-0.1)   -1.0 (-0.9)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1    (0.5)    2.8  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -0.1    (0.0)    2.3  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1    (0.0)    0.1  (0.1)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.6    (0.0)    3.3  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2    (0.0)    0.9  (0.7)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     2.9   (-0.1)    5.5  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    4.6  (4.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.3    (1.2)    1.1  (0.9)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1    (1.5)    1.7  (1.5)</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
